{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462756-how-many-tzimisce-antediluvians-there-are-other-antes-too","id":1462756,"title":"How Many Tzimisce Antediluvians there are? (other Antes too)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-04T20:47:55-07:00","id":1462756,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> How Many Tzimisce Antediluvians there are? (other Antes too)","content":"I mean, sometimes, it looks like some Antediluvians are more than in one place at the same time, and that would be fine, but mostly it is treated as 'one of this just can't be it', but the case where this is least apparent is the Eldest Tzimisce. And i would like to keep track of the blood sucker mess, before I tried to list the others.<br /> <br /> TZIMISCE ELDEST LINES<br /> \u2022Well, first there seems to be only one, that was in the First City and all that, and then went to Transylvania and made dealings with Kupala, maybe freeing it and getting some power in return, but anyway, it survived the Deluge. After it, during the Second Baali War, Samiel went to him and killed the old bastard, and he took Samiel down with him. The bogatyri left and went to the four corners (supposedly each carry a bit of his flesh, so there's already wide plausible opportunity). It seems though, the Eldest's most core self germinated in the womb of Dracon, his favored childe, which shows that he is capable of doing this switch (although it might only be possible to do in direct children who are powerful enough to sustain it). After a hard pregnancy to say the least, the dead father-child was born and Dracon gave it to Yorak and his Cathedral of Flesh. All this happened in Ancient Times. [I call this form the &quot;<b>Cathedralic</b>&quot; one]<br /> <br /> \u2022We got then an interesting albeit disconnected one, that is the god-tree form, that was under the care of Damek Ruthvan in his Sarmizegetusa domain, where a giant labyrinthian forest lies within a mountain of sorts. There is a tree there, that, in 1232(33) Ilias cel Frumos, when he was there with Myca Vykos and Malachite searching for info on Nikita of Sredetz, a huge old-ass tree that emanates what Ilias, a koldun sorcerer, believes is the power of a god, and when he is embracing it (more the tree embracing him) he asks what this god wants, but it couldn't respond, but gave him a red seed. Some time later, when Nikita of Sredetz (actually Dracon) faced the three (Ilias, Vykos, Malachite) plus Markus Musa Giovanni, Ilias had the previous night (or so) eaten the seed in a ritual looking for answers. So, when Dracon appeared he recognized not Ilias, but his creator, the Tzimisce Eldest. I'm a bit confused who is simply destroyed and who is melded together by the Eldest, but Ilias self is destroyed (and supposedly his body turns to ash for it can't contain the power of the elder for long), but I assume the Eldest turned Dracon and Vykos into balls of flesh and ate them (he does this to Vykos at least), so... Ilias, Vykos and Dracon, plus something if not the whole of the Eldest become one. It seems the purpose of the Eldest was meld Dracon with someone who wanted to live, because Dracon wanted to die, but the Eldest wanted him to live on. So we might say Vykos is carrying or is in some form the Eldest. <br /> This goes in three hypothesis then; <i>First</i>, the god-tree might have been given to the Ruthvans by Yorak, since they are a family who cares for the Eldest, so it would be the Cathedralic one turned into what I would call the &quot;<b>Arboreal</b>&quot; one. <i>Second</i>, the Eldest still lives partially as the Arboreal one, even if it gave one part of itself to Ilias. <i>Third </i>is that the Eldest didn't simply got destroyed after it imparted Dracon in Vykos, but actually is part of Vykos as well (which at this point might as well be Sascha Vykos).<br /> All in all there might be one Eldest, the Cathedralic that was given to the Ruthvens and made into the Arboreal one, which then lives on as Vykos. There might also be a Cathedralic one that lives as the Cathedral of Flesh, an Arboreal one that lives in Damek's domain yet, and one that lives in Vykos. Technically, at least one must be true, but all could be.<br /> <br /> \u2022Alright now, last one is the Eldest who was in Sernog Monastery in 1413, when Lugoj Blood-Breaker, Lambach, Velya and other Anarchs (and technically the Transylvania Chronicles PCs too) raided the place, killed its guardians and Lugoj diablerized the Eldest in human form. First, they found this location because Lambach Ruthven knew the place, his family being one that always served the Eldest closely (with all that possibility that Lambach does all he does in purpose, and isn't simply an idiot coward, but it doesn't matter that much). Second, Lugoj didn't diablerise shit, sometime, some place (possibly during the raid on the monastery), the Eldest impaled the sucker on a wooden hook, took Lugoj's form, and created a dummy of an Antediluvian who he diablerized for the appearance of a successful Anarch incursion. He made a brief speech and went into torpor shortly after, calling Lambach &quot;a good lad&quot;, for he knew everything but couldn't bring himself to say it at the time. I call this the &quot;<b>Monastic</b>&quot; one, and its origins aren't clear for me. Either way, &quot;Lugoj&quot; (Eldest) was taken much later by the Zantosa revenants to NYC underground, where he basically turned into Kars from Jojo and tried every single living thing on Earth, basically trying to achieve the Metamorphosists dream goal. Becoming the giant flesh beast that ate Lambach's arm when he went down there to see it. This Eldest was being taken care of by powerful Tzimisces, one of which was the then dead ilias cel Frumos, according to Beckett's Jihad Diary. But the Antediluvian form skipped town, and nobody knows where he went.<br /> So... what Eldest went to the Sernog Monastery? The Cathedralic? Did it matured into an independent form nurtured by Yorak and the Cathedral of Flesh? Was it all just like a new extension of the Cathedral of Flesh planted there in Sernog and didn't actually had a human form until it disguised itself as Lugoj? Because it couldn't be the (possible) one that Vykos had in himself. So it could be the Arboreal one, but that was replanted there in Sernog Monastery, maybe just a new seed that the Ruthven family planted there and it turned into a new form (the Monastic) that did all the Lugoj switcharoo. Either way, this form went to become the most famous and freaky mountain of flesh in the subways of NYC for most of The Masquerade's metaplot. <br /> <br /> -Possible Forms:<br /> 1. Any of the flesh bits that the dispersed Bogatyri carried.<br /> 2. Any of his childer of the 4th Generation.<br /> 3. The <b>Cathedralic </b>one purely (a dead fetus basically) that was cared by Yorak.<br /> 4. Part of the Cathedral of Flesh, that ended up eating Yorak in 1493.<br /> 5. The <b>Arboreal </b>one in Damek's Ruthven domain.<br /> 6. Part of Sascha Vykos, since 1232 or 1233.<br /> 7. Fake Lugoj's sprawling form in the USA, the <b>Monastic</b> one.<br /> <br /> so yeah, people, what do you think? 1 and 2 are cheating basically, but which you think are more true? are any of my three main lines wrong or misinterpreted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T22:13:11-07:00","id":1462762,"title":"","content":"I may be wrong, but I remember something about when Ilias fought Dracon a body being found in that place and put into the monastery. So it may be that instead of going to Vykos it went to the monastery (or just split again). I'm also almost sure that the thing in the sewers isn't necessarily the same as Fake Lugoj's body, as far as anyone knows that body is still there in torpor (although it may just have left and no one noticed, I don't think anyone opens the sarcophagus every day just to kiss him good night).<br /> <br /> Well, the answer obviously depends on what you want to make of him in a chronicle, but the fate of the eldest is one of the most interesting among the Antes because instead of a lack of information we have too much. It boils down to a chain of questions: can it split up in more selfs? If yes, when did it acquired this ability?<br /> <br /> But if the first answer is no, then the Eldest may be anyone of those or none, and yet every single one is itself a relic of great power created by the Eldest, so at no point the information becomes irrelevant.<br /> <br /> So I'd say our options are:<br /> 1. The flesh carried by the Bogatyri;<br /> 2. The Cathedralic Fetus;<br /> 3. The Cathedral of Flesh itself;<br /> 4. The Arboreal;<br /> 5. The thing in Vykos;<br /> 6. The Monastic fake Lugoj;<br /> 7. The Thing in the Sewers;<br /> 8. The 4th generation Childe in some way;<br /> 9. Vicissitude.<br /> <br /> My personal take, as I like less OP takes on the Antes, is that it is currently either just the body in the monastery or the thing in the Sewer, and in this last case not necessarily as much in control as it wanted to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T05:55:48-07:00","id":1462794,"title":"","content":"I always liked the notion from Revised that the True Antediluvians (i.e. the genuine pre-flood variety not late-comer diablerists like Tremere and Giovanni) were all looking for ways to transcend their vampiric state\u2026 Malkav became the Malkavian Madness Network. Ennoia earthmelded into the heart of the world and, heck, might be acting as substitute Gaia at this stage if the W5 stuff where the original was ganked during the Apocalypse is true. Lasombra became the Abyss.<br /> <br /> In that version Tzimisce became Vicissitude (basically taking the soul-eater concept and applying it to the Founder\u2019s plans for trancendence). There is no single Tzimisce, just his will subtlely guided every practitioner of his Art.<br /> <br /> I mean, Saulot has divided his consciousness into at least two vessels\u2026 it\u2019s not exactly a crazy notion that virtually all of the original Antediluvians have either died or transcended by now and what\u2019s left are just shells, pretenders and a couple of oddballs who couldn\u2019t get their acts together and actually aren\u2019t any more potent than a Methuselah as a result.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see;<br /> - Haqim: unknown<br /> - Brujah: diablerized early, Troile in torpor beneath salted earth of Carthage.<br /> - Ennoia: merged with the Earth and became something else.<br /> - Lasombra: merged with the Abyss and became something else.<br /> - Malkav: became the Madness Network.<br /> - Absimiliard: possibly Obfuscated himself out of existence\u2026 or sitting at the bottom of the ocean making monsters.<br /> - Ravnos: may have become something more, but was obliterated by plot device.<br /> - Arikel/Ishtar: may or may not be porn star in Hollywood (it\u2019s so ridiculous it must be true).<br /> - Saulot: possibly split into white worm and child.<br /> - Cappadocius: partially diablerized and became spectre, possibly as part of failed plan to diablerize God.<br /> - Tzimisce: became Vicissitude inside every practitioner.<br /> - Ventru/Typhon: probably diablerized by Set and absorbing him may have resulted in a composite personality Set-Typhon.<br /> <br /> That would account for all the 13 Clans (with a couple of unknowns), but is technically one Antediluvian short. If you wanted to run with it, I\u2019d suggest Haqim and Absimiliard having achieved some type of transcendence such that only the lost hedonist Arikel and the latecomers still banging about as corporeal entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T10:39:05-07:00","id":1462809,"title":"","content":"Limiting The Eldest's possession to just Its immediate childer, what a generous interpretation! I've always leaned more towards the idea that literally anything that has been touched by the blood of Tzimisce is, theoretically, a possible vector for the Antediluvian. IIRC you have to taste the blood of a vampire that knows a Discipline before it is possible to learn the Discipline itself? In practice, that means every Vicissitude user has likely been exposed, but hypothetically I could conceive of another Vicissitude-using Ancient that could be distinct bloodline. I don't imagine the Eldest as Vicissitude Itself, but rather the master of the Discipline to such an extent that It might as well be.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I care as much about trying to nail down how many forms the Eldest might be split between, but to respond to the examples listed above:<br /> <br /> I've always considered the original Cathedral of Flesh more as a distinct entity than an extension of the Eldest. As vulnerable to domination by the Eldest as anything else Vicissitude based, most likely, but not anymore a specific part of the Eldest Itself than Yorak or anything else linked to it by blood.<br /> <br /> I tend to view the God-Tree as a phase, an early experiment comparable to what ended up happening under New York, trying to figure out if it could cheat the limits of the Curse by assuming a radically different biology. I had always assumed It eventually took on a different shape and left, but I haven't read the Clan Novels so there could be a bunch that I am missing.<br /> <br /> Continuing from the &quot;never read the novel&quot; point, my knowledge of what happened with Vykos, the Dracon, and the Eldest/Ilias is rather limited. But I tended to assume that what was put into Vykos was primarily the Dracon, not the Eldest Itself. But then, my views about the omnipresence of the Eldest in Its bloodline make the idea of it &quot;putting itself&quot; into Vykos rather redundant.<br /> <br /> I don't think I ever really considered the question of whether or not the Eldest still parades Its Lugoj-suit around sometimes, to reinforce the idea that It's gone. I probably ended up assuming continuity, generally: that the Eldest reborn from the Dracon became the God-Tree, which eventually became Fake-Lugoj, which eventually became The Thing Beneath New York.<br /> <br /> A related question, one I find rather interesting and suggests a significant shift in the portrayal of the Eldest, has to do with the reappearance of Ilias in BJD. Is the Eldest just walking around in an Ilias-suit for some inscrutable reason? Or did the Eldest actually resurrect Its descendant? Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T11:54:25-07:00","id":1462819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462756-how-many-tzimisce-antediluvians-there-are-other-antes-too?p=1462809#post1462809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Limiting The Eldest's possession to just Its immediate childer, what a generous interpretation! I've always leaned more towards the idea that literally anything that has been touched by the blood of Tzimisce is, theoretically, a possible vector for the Antediluvian.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAlthough I can get behind the idea of an Ante evolving to somehow &quot;touch&quot; its descendants, like the Makavian Network, I'm generally against the idea of them being too much in control over every descendant.<br /> <br /> This is still an RPG and we can have players of all clans. I've already saw in <i>Nights of Prophecy</i> the &quot;brilliant&quot; approach of a PC being insta-killed for no other crime than being of the wrong clan for the story. This is a shitty plot device I want to stir away from. Being the Discipline and manifesting through it to some extent is good. Being able to possess a character so thoroughly as to turn a clan unplayable if the Ante is used, not so much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462756-how-many-tzimisce-antediluvians-there-are-other-antes-too?p=1462794#post1462794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Haqim: unknown<br /> - Brujah: diablerized early, Troile in torpor beneath salted earth of Carthage.<br /> - Ennoia: merged with the Earth and became something else.<br /> - Lasombra: merged with the Abyss and became something else.<br /> - Malkav: became the Madness Network.<br /> - Absimiliard: possibly Obfuscated himself out of existence\u2026 or sitting at the bottom of the ocean making monsters.<br /> - Ravnos: may have become something more, but was obliterated by plot device.<br /> - Arikel/Ishtar: may or may not be porn star in Hollywood (it\u2019s so ridiculous it must be true).<br /> - Saulot: possibly split into white worm and child.<br /> - Cappadocius: partially diablerized and became spectre, possibly as part of failed plan to diablerize God.<br /> - Tzimisce: became Vicissitude inside every practitioner.<br /> - Ventru/Typhon: probably diablerized by Set and absorbing him may have resulted in a composite personality Set-Typhon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind the idea of one or more Antes living rather mundane lives in modern days, and I would say that those are actually the winners, as other either sacrificed their sense of Self or simply can't extricate themselves from the Jyhad and the general horror anymore.<br /> <br /> But the idea of Arikel living as a pornstar just for the lols? That's childish and disgusting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T12:23:53-07:00","id":1462822,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, I've forgotten to add up and important factor here, and that is the fact that Lugoj's and Velya's and perhaps more importantly Lambach's blood were used in consonance with Kupala's Sacred Flower for the first Vaulderie, that is like a patient zero. I mean... this was basically a realization for me that ALL FREAKING SABBAT is liable to the whims of the Eldest or at the very least Kupala, even if the Vicissitude vector lies dormant and unusable by the carriers. But I don't imagine most Cainites being able to hold the Eldest in their body, it's just too much power (even if we go by a low power scale for Antes).<br /> <br /> And one thing that is interesting to notice is that... most Antes, funnily enough don't seem to suffer from their Weakness. Perhaps only Absimiliard does... The Eldest basically went everywhere, so either by Disciplines, or by carrying a grain of his native soil everywhere in his organs, or whatever; or by making a pact with Kupala; or simply having one of his forms in Transylvania while the others do god knows what is and example, a complex one at that maybe.<br /> <br /> One I still find very weird is the <b>Tremere </b>one (that I forgot too!) I mean... just what happened? After the ritual of usurpation and all but Tremere not wanting to tear Goratrix to bits, they were vampires, but supposedly they would be either Tzimisce (and that is fidly because yeah, freaking magic, not Embrace, makes things strange) or Caitiff. I mean, if it worked out like Embrace, they would be 9th generation, for they made a childe of Vladimir (who is 6th gen) Embrace Goratrix's apprentices (so they were 8th gen) and then ate the poor bastards and kind of Embrace themselves. So who knows if they were already carriers of the Eldest, cuz this was so fucking extraordinary that it could go any way. We may only suppose that Tremere diablerized other Tzimisces before doing Saulot in. But even if not, only after Tremere turned 3rd Generation did the Eldest start being a nuisance and petty fight with Saulot. I think the whole Tremere internal arch is a freaking mess, and it seemed gratuitous to throw the Eldest in almost out of nowhere. But yeah, there is this &quot;other&quot; Eldest in here. And who knows, by the 21st century it seems only Saulot inhabits Tremere's original body, with the Eldest probably giving a lot of trouble still. But, they might be all destroyed with the Vienna cleanup by the SI. <br /> <br /> <br /> And yeah XD it isn't as much that I want a precise number, but wanted to try to keep track of the most certain possibilities and which are more interesting. Besides the fact that lore-dwelling and theorizing is fun, I think, like the thread about who is Typhon, what is the nature of Set or Sutekh etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T13:36:17-07:00","id":1462829,"title":"","content":"I personally consider the Tremere as not being really Cainites, since to me it is more interesting if their ritual is really something too distant from an Embrace, and they were already fairly old and powerful as Mages, it would be silly for them to be just drinking blood and getting a &quot;common&quot; Embrace. It was a complex alchemical concoction with enough power to convince seven Masters (maybe Archmages) that it wouldn't affect them with an aspect of the curse they were already quite aware of.<br /> <br /> So it would make sense that the concoction didn't contained actual blood, and even if it did that Goratrix did manage to distill and eliminate a truly powerful curse from there. Since it wasn't the Curse of Caine, it may well have been the essence of the Eldest. To me they aren't a bloodline or clan, they're something else that play by similar rules. It is even possible that what kept them so similar to actual Kindred was the will of an Ante, maybe Saulot already messing with them even then.<br /> <br /> Given that soul manipulation is Saulot's shtick, the Eldest wouldn't stay in this other Ante's playground for long anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T13:36:43-07:00","id":1462830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462756-how-many-tzimisce-antediluvians-there-are-other-antes-too?p=1462819#post1462819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bAlthough I can get behind the idea of an Ante evolving to somehow &quot;touch&quot; its descendants, like the Makavian Network, I'm generally against the idea of them being too much in control over every descendant.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is still an RPG and we can have players of all clans. I've already saw in <i>Nights of Prophecy</i> the &quot;brilliant&quot; approach of a PC being insta-killed for no other crime than being of the wrong clan for the story. This is a shitty plot device I want to stir away from. Being the Discipline and manifesting through it to some extent is good. Being able to possess a character so thoroughly as to turn a clan unplayable if the Ante is used, not so much.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I don't mind the idea of one or more Antes living rather mundane lives in modern days, and I would say that those are actually the winners, as other either sacrificed their sense of Self or simply can't extricate themselves from the Jyhad and the general horror anymore.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But the idea of Arikel living as a pornstar just for the lols? That's childish and disgusting.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's fair, and I'm not trying to suggest that the Eldest is controlling all of its descendants all of the time, but rather that the potential is planted. And I think there could be circumstances that would allow someone with Tzimisce blood to resist, or even escape, the control of the Eldest. Two examples that spring to mind are infernalism or Golconda.<br /> <br /> I like my Antediluvians as god-like, but fallible and vulnerable under some circumstances.<br /> <br /> Regarding the fates of the others, I'm not really on board with adding Absimiliard to the list of &quot;transcended&quot; Antediluvians. I like the characterization of him as a vain, petty prick who was too busy plotting vengeance or sulking to try and overcome his Curse. Haqim is an interesting case, because Quietus as power-over-the-Blood has interesting implications for a path similar to the Eldest, though it's a bit muddled by it also being a grab-bag of assassin-stuff. But I don't know if that's the vibe I get from what I've read about Haqim. I've heard the theory about Ventrue/Typhon, not entirely sure that I'm sold, but I've never quite decided if I wanted Ventrue dead or not; I find the whole &quot;decided to just peace out from the whole Jyhad with uber-level Dominate and Presence&quot; theory kind of entertaining.<br /> <br /> My favourite pet theory for Saulot and Tremere at the moment has Saulot using something like Cret's Thaumaturgy Ritual that lets a vampire split between Man and Beast/Hun and P'o after slipping out of Golconda. And Tremere gobbled P'o-lot. Which may or may not have been part of a Just As Planned by P'o-lot in what is possibly a millennia-long struggle between the two halves of Saulot.<br /> <br /> Which source has Arikel as a porn star?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T14:11:56-07:00","id":1462837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1462756-how-many-tzimisce-antediluvians-there-are-other-antes-too?p=1462830#post1462830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the fates of the others, I'm not really on board with adding Absimiliard to the list of &quot;transcended&quot; Antediluvians. I like the characterization of him as a vain, petty prick who was too busy plotting vengeance or sulking to try and overcome his Curse. Haqim is an interesting case, because Quietus as power-over-the-Blood has interesting implications for a path similar to the Eldest, though it's a bit muddled by it also being a grab-bag of assassin-stuff. But I don't know if that's the vibe I get from what I've read about Haqim. I've heard the theory about Ventrue/Typhon, not entirely sure that I'm sold, but I've never quite decided if I wanted Ventrue dead or not; I find the whole &quot;decided to just peace out from the whole Jyhad with uber-level Dominate and Presence&quot; theory kind of entertaining.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree on most of this. Absimiliard would be an interesting exploration of the primary Kindred impulse: grab power, grab resources, but in the end you're to petty to become anything more than the little, insignificant person you have always been. You could say that his entire clan grew to be more meaningful than him. And that is a destiny waiting for many masters of the Jyhad, powerful movers and shakers, sure, but in the end they exist for the Jyhad and not the opposite, they're too petty to really transcend.<br /> <br /> Haqim have the problem that his development as character/myth is far later from the development of his clan and discipline as more than <i>Bad Arab Archetype</i>. So yes, it is hard to reconcile completely Quietus with Haqim. Indeed, I'm not sure if I would even try to, it strikes me as interesting for Quietus to be a later development by the Sorcerers. If we get the three castes and isolate sorcery and Quietus, we get a spread of Auspex, Celerity and Obfuscate that could be original to him.<br /> <br /> Ventrue is the ultimate player of the Jyhad, but the Jyhad is a rigged game. The only way to win is to not play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T15:28:05-07:00","id":1462840,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Absimiliard has been one of the most temporal and bitter Antediluvians for sure. These are interesting thoughts. <br /> One interesting thing is I believe, through a Christian lens that the main end goal of many Antediluvians is the one thing almost every WoD line has, transcendence. And well, there might be some of those that reached the doors but for goodness or doubt turned back (like the idea of bodhisattvas that &quot;stayed&quot; to guide others). Like yeah, the Curse of Caine leaves you in a Purgatorial existence, where you can either evolve, repent or debase yourself further. Of course, to transcend might be to Heaven, to Godhood, to Demonhood, to Hell, to Cosmos, or something like that, whatever; be it Road of Heaven or Metamorphosis.<br /> <br /> Absimiliard is spiteful lil shit and wants just to make everyone suffer for his hubris and mistakes (if we follow this default interpretation). Saulot being divided in at least two entities of rationale and instinct makes a lot of sense for me. Especially if we believe that weird child form in Hunedoara is the rationale one (Hun, right?), and the Tremere-bound one the instinctual one (P'o). Yet there seems to be one or more form of Saulot? Or maybe I'm remembering it wrong. I always wondered how antitribu Salubri would interact with Saulomere if they actually managed to come face-to-face; would be conversion, destructive hate, complete shock and despair, fear?<br /> <br /> And yeah, I believe Ventru/Veddartha (I know the second name is technically a childer but goddamn I love that name for an Antediluvian) kind of made a sacrifice of sorts. I mean, he would be a master of self, and the Hindi and Buddhist parallels are there, so he might've transcended as a welding power to all his childer; like, a Malk Network but one that works more like a Vinculum Network, that helped Ventrue through history mostly work together instead of killing itself. That or something more Jyhad bastardly evil plan. I really don't believe he just up and died in front of the gates of the First City (or Second, don't remember). The Brujahs denial of any foul play from their part is kinda weird too, even more so because they shouldn't care of any accusation. <br /> Troile too was a bit tad temporal, or simply loved Earth too much, or maybe was just too impatient and feeling to achieve the control for any form of transcendence, so he/she chose to drown in abandonment. Ennoia seems to be gone, simply gone, wherever she went (if she'll be back I assume only if and when the Eldest or Absimiliard or Set comes up knocking shit up). Lasombra seems to be pure part of the Abyss but somehow maintained so form of autonomy (Malfean or Neverborn levels maybe? or something different). Arikel I like to think is stuck somewhere, either in a dream of something the real world is incapable of making, or at something or someone so enveloping she can't move from it. Ravana, Set, Haqim, Malk, and most other seems to be either beyond individuality, or are in a single body. I believe Ravana kind became part of maya, or something like that, going with the vibe that Antes exist through the Blood and Arts of their childer; and yeah, the Week of Nightmares thing was his body in wassail, an empty husk with a nuclear ravenous dog let loose. <br /> <br /> Cappadocius is an interesting one, and an Ante I particularly like. Besides the many identities he went through, it seems in 1444 his body was destroyed. His soul went to the Shadowlands, and he somehow managed to separate his Shadow from his Wraith, and the specter caused a lot of shenanigans. Maybe his &quot;higher soul&quot; really did went to somewhere and only his Specter remained. I mean, is kind of fun to imagine the thickening of the Veil, and all the Stasisation of the world and the spirit world (at least for the &quot;&quot;Western Cultures&quot;&quot;) came because, or in addition to, Cappadocius taking down or being taken down by God. XD <br /> Either way, his influence was dropped way too hastily I think. Only his steps were left as something important to people to go after. Apotheosis right? Although Ambrogino, the lil bastard, did summoned and bound his Specter in the Black Monastery and Beckett.... seems like unbound it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T16:19:40-07:00","id":1462842,"title":"","content":"Saulot isn't in two places, canonically he went to Hunedoara after the end of the struggle in Tremere's body, so he probably just left the Tremere and got there. He does have another possible body in one of the Gehenna scenarios, but is actually a clone. Although the idea of his soul splitting isn't impossible, it isn't the simplest interpretation of canon and I think it is a little heavy-handed.<br /> <br /> He is too much himself, anyway. With all the stories about him you see Saulot wandering all over the place, starting self-sustaining projects and leaving to start the next. He doesn't seem to have transcended and actually to focus too much on anything. And whatever interpretation you have of him, he's extremely intelligent, but far from infallible. I'd say he is still just a kindred, although more powerful than any Methuselah, that wanders about messing with the Jyhad more than playing it, still trying to find a way to collective kindred transcendence that keeps eluding him, master of many roads and satisfied with none.<br /> <br /> I just had an idea about Veddartha, that instead of transcendence through his clan or Discipline, he did it through the idea of vampiric government. Keeping in mind that I find V5 Camarilla abhorrent and don't use it, Veddartha could be living in the very idea of it, a living concept guiding the Inner Council. He doesn't command the union of all vampires, he IS.<br /> <br /> Lasombra depends a lot on what you think the Abyss is, as many things carry this name in WoD. But I don't think becoming one with it would be a good idea. I've always went by the idea that he either absorbed something there and left, or was consumed there by something else that may or may not care about vampires now. And given how in Demon &quot;God&quot; is absent, it would be interesting to assume that he actually achieved apotheosis and ate God, for whatever that means, long ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T16:25:18-07:00","id":1462843,"title":"","content":"I'll never run a chronicle where the Antedeluvians are close enough to center stage for it to matter, but my headcanon regarding Haqim has it that the resemblance between the Alamut blood well that powers his clan's sorcery and the Baali's wells of sacrifice is no idle coincidence. Taken alongside the legend that Haqim ushered in his clan's sorcerer caste specifically to fight the Baali, I like to think it's possible that Haqim and Saulot might have been rivals competing for the favor of the same masters since at least the Second City.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I think Haqim's been hiding down at the bottom of that well, possibly since the 2nd Century C.E. since that was the last time anyone outside his clan saw him.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of Arikel being held in reverie somewhere, possibly transfixed by something beautiful of her own creation; and of Absimiliard being the one who's too petty to evolve much at all. It suits the idea of the Nosferatu being the really human ones underneath it all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 10-05-2021, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T18:23:46-07:00","id":1462848,"title":"","content":"I too think Sutekh, Haqim and Saulot would in some way meet. They have that wandering philosopher warrior vibe to them. I do think though there is some kind of pact, maybe just the Traditions, bounding them in some way, like they can't meet (or can but fucking hate themselves), but can't act against each other, so the Jyhad is the indirect manner with which they do so. And hell, maybe they want to ally themselves and put father dearest down, or some project made together (even if not all of them) but holly damn, is it hard to give orders to people you don't know and have centuries and continents away of distance between, so everything is a big bombastic mess. <br /> <br /> I actually like the closed up, scheming, sheltered, p.o.s, elite with religious and corporate style of V5 Camarilla, and think it doesn't necessarily mean open war with Anarchs always, so things don't need to be much different just a bit more delineated. But Veddartha incorporating ideals like that is somewhat I imagined, so I can agree with that.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce Eldest I think, if it is not satisfied with its many forms, will probably look for its brothers and sisters, so it can be whole. At least the amorphous form... The others are dormant maybe. <br /> <br /> And I think that Haqim is the most like Caine, and probably the only one besides Malkav that he would meet. I always had this idea, but it never seems to have any canon indication (which isn't relevant of course). So okay, if Saulot isn't divided, we have half of Cappadocius, a multitude of Tzimisce, and either missing individuals Antes, and gone ethereal or dispersed Antes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T21:16:27-07:00","id":1462869,"title":"","content":"One interesting element to ponder is, if the Antes are almost entirely transcended or just really not in the picture\u2026 who or what is actually behind the Beckoning and the cyclical Gehenna? Is it actually the 4th Gen seeking enough power to supplant or join the Antediluvians? Is it just the few Antediluvians who are capable of corporeal action? Is it perhaps one or more of the not-so-dead after all 2nd Generation?<br /> <br /> And what of the Stoneman? Supposedly he is the oldest Caitiff in existence\u2026 except the real first Clanless is actually Caine himself (as were his Childer). So is the Stoneman actually Caine working behind the scenes to bring down the Sects (which has all sorts of cosmically funny implications for the Sabbat)? One of the Second Generation? One of the oldest Methuselahs sired when the blood was still thin enough to result in the absence of the Curse? Perhaps a 4th Gen who predated the murder of the Second Generation and took no part in it and so evaded the very curses that define the clans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-05T22:23:19-07:00","id":1462872,"title":"","content":"Transcendence doesn't have to mean an Ante left the Jyhad, just that this Ante isn't merely taking part on it for the sake of it. Malkav, Veddartha and the Eldest are some that may have any sort of ulterior reason to do it. It is actually simpler to think it is a move from them than from a &quot;lesser&quot; Ante, as those would mostly still play by kindred rules, and so a power like the Beckoning doesn't make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> Caine himself or members of the Second Generation may be behind it, but other things too. Demons, spirits, God, Angels. When we talk about Gehenna we're not just talking about Antedilluvians, but about the orgins and end of the curse, its purpose, and as such about the things that predated vampirism altogether, whatever they are.<br /> <br /> It can even be a species-wide instinct, from time to time Kindred that meet certain criteria have this compulsion and it serves some evolutionary purpose. Mystical or not, the force behind the Beckoning doesn't even need to be a character, an entity with recognizable identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}